 17592186045498 13194139534119 17592186045417 true] [17592186410821 1083 #uuid "b2e66482-ad5e-56f0-ab9c-0187ad900545" 13194139534119 17592186045417 true] [17592186410822 1080 "(8,-9)" 13194139534119 17592186045417 true] [17592186410822 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534119 17592186045417 true] [17592186410822 1083 #uuid "c15d36f2-d954-5b67-a997-5ab2ddb7afaa" 13194139534119 17592186045417 true] [17592186410823 1075 #edb/ref 17592186410818 13194139534119 17592186045417 true] [17592186410823 1075 #edb/ref 17592186410819 13194139534119 17592186045417 true] [17592186410823 1075 #edb/ref 17592186410820 13194139534119 17592186045417 true] [17592186410823 1075 #edb/ref 17592186410821 13194139534119 17592186045417 true] [17592186410823 1075 #edb/ref 17592186410822 13194139534119 17592186045417 true] [17592186410823 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534119 17592186045417 true] [17592186410823 1077 "selection" 13194139534119 17592186045417 true] [17592186410823 1078 #edb/ref 17592186410818 13194139534119 17592186045417 true] [17592186410823 1079 #uuid "236f2410-bb87-524a-b10a-c030da587949" 13194139534119 17592186045417 true] [17592186410824 1068 #edb/ref 17592186410823 13194139534119 17592186045417 true] [17592186410824 1069 "q-126900" 13194139534119 17592186045417 true] [17592186410824 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534119 17592186045417 true] [17592186410824 1071 "Given the curve $r(t)=⟨{t}^{2}-2t,4t-1⟩,$ find the point at which the tangent to the curve is parallel to the vector $⟨-1,1⟩.$" 13194139534119 17592186045417 true] [17592186410824 1072 #uuid "eb19afc5-d677-5f22-bac0-92428e650b61" 13194139534119 17592186045417 true] [17592186410824 1074 "First, we calculate the derivative of $r(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}-2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4t-1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t-2,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $⟨-1\\,,\\,1⟩$ are parallel for some specific value ${t}_{0}$ of the parameter $t$ if and only if there exists a constant $c$ such that ${r}^{′}({t}_{0})=c⟨-1,1⟩.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =c⟨-1,1⟩ \\\\ ⟨2t-2,4⟩ & =c⟨-1,1⟩ \\\\ ⟨2t-2,4⟩ & =⟨-c,c⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the components gives:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2t-2=-c \\\\ 4=c\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we obtain that $c=4.$ Substituting $c=4$ into the first equation, we get $t=-1.$ \n\nTherefore, $⟨-1,1⟩$ and ${r}^{′}$ are parallel only at the point corresponding to $t=-1.$\n\nFinally, since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(-1) & =⟨(-1)^{2}-2(-1),4(-1)-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,-5⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe conclude that $⟨-1,1⟩$ and ${r}^{′}(t)$ are parallel at the point $(3,-5).$" 13194139534119 17592186045417 true] [17592186410825 1058 #edb/ref 17592186410828 13194139534119 17592186045417 true] [17592186410825 1062 #uuid "25cc0c4b-5364-577c-92a1-008375ee5f34" 13194139534119 17592186045417 true] [17592186410825 1063 #edb/ref 17592186410824 13194139534119 17592186045417 true] [17592186410826 1058 #edb/ref 17592186410825 13194139534119 17592186045417 true] [17592186410826 1062 #uuid "588c5c9a-8d3d-51b8-8b90-dff365fed144" 13194139534119 17592186045417 true] [17592186410826 1063 #edb/ref 17592186345046 13194139534119 17592186045417 true] [17592186410827 1058 #edb/ref 17592186410829 13194139534119 17592186045417 true] [17592186410827 1062 #uuid "677b5852-f95c-533d-b31c-e87dce9ad2d7" 13194139534119 17592186045417 true] [17592186410827 1063 #edb/ref 17592186284525 13194139534119 17592186045417 true] [17592186410828 1058 #edb/ref 17592186410827 13194139534119 17592186045417 true] [17592186410828 1062 #uuid "881f99cb-89c3-507b-a7a0-8ef265378f7b" 13194139534119 17592186045417 true] [17592186410828 1063 #edb/ref 17592186120109 13194139534119 17592186045417 true] [17592186410829 1062 #uuid "c80e8392-766a-5d4f-9dc1-c5ef5cb2463f" 13194139534119 17592186045417 true] [17592186410829 1063 #edb/ref 17592186284532 13194139534119 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"activity-27a466